    "long_instructions": "**It’s time to make the thermostat more intelligent.**\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:** \r\n- Update the program so it always turns to the most preferred temperature.\r\n- Make sure `turn` always prints one of `\"UP\"`, `\"STAY\"`, or `\"DOWN\"`.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nRemember, you can compare the value of parameters using a conditional statement. These can include `if`, `elif`, and `else` statements.\r\n\r\n```python\r\nif up > current:\r\n    ...\r\nelif down > current:\r\n    ...\r\nelse:\r\n    ...\r\n```\r\n",
